# Git Commit & Push Policy

## Agent permissions (hard ceiling)

| Command | Agent |
|---|---|
| `git add` (stage) | ✅ In `/start-coding` only — files for current sub-task/phase |
| `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` | ✅ Read-only — any stage |
| `git commit` | ❌ **Never** — user runs in their terminal |
| `git push` | ❌ **Never** — unless user **explicitly** asks to push in the same message |
| `git push --force` | ❌ **Never** — unless user explicitly requests (warn on main/master) |

**Why:** Commits must keep the requester's git author (e.g. `viet-le-ship`), not Cursor AI.

## When the user commits

| Stage | Commands | Who commits |
|---|---|---|
| 1–2 | `/analyze-task`, `/grooming` | ❌ Nobody — no commit |
| 3–5 | `/write-spec`, `/recheck-spec`, `/check-spec` | ❌ Nobody — working tree only |
| 6 | `/breakdown-task` | ❌ Nobody |
| 7 | `/start-coding` | ❌ Agent stages only (`git add`) |
| 8 | `/review-staged` | ✅ **User** — after READY verdict, copy command agent prints |
| 9 | `/recheck-release`, `/create-pr` | ❌ Nobody — artifacts only; **no push** |

## Implementation loop (Stages 7–8)

```
/start-coding → implement one phase/sub-task → git add (agent)
  → /review-staged
  → if BLOCKED: fix → re-stage → /review-staged again
  → if READY: agent prints commit command → user runs git commit in terminal
  → next phase/sub-task
```

**One phase / sub-task → one commit** (user creates it after READY).

## `/review-staged` commit gate (READY only)

When verdict is **READY** (no 🔴/🟠):

1. **DO NOT** run `git commit`.
2. Print a **copy-ready block** for the user:

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
<type>(<scope>): <summary>
EOF
)"
```

3. Remind: run in **your terminal** so author stays yours.
4. Optional: print `git log -1 --format='%an %ae'` after user confirms they committed.

If verdict is **BLOCKED** — do not print a commit command.

## Commit message format

Default: `.agents/skills/pr-conventions/SKILL.md` — Conventional Commits, English, imperative.

**Multi-phase features** (e.g. No.96 property-ui — land / house series / house option):

```
feat(<scope>): part <N>: <area> - <imperative summary>
```

Examples:

```
feat(property-ui): part 1: house series - update CSS for name
feat(property-ui): part 2: land - scope routes under properties
```

- `<N>` = phase or PR number from `/breakdown-task`
- `<area>` = `land`, `house series`, `house option`, etc.
- One phase → one commit

Typical types in implementation loop: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `style` — not `docs` for spec-only work during Stages 3–5.

## Spec phase (Stages 3–5)

- Edit BD/DDD in the **working tree only** — no commit required for `Status: FINAL`.
- Default: keep spec uncommitted until user chooses to include in a phase commit.

## Agent hard rules

1. **NEVER** run `git commit` in any stage — including `/review-staged` READY.
2. **NEVER** run `git push` unless the user explicitly requests push in the same message.
3. **NEVER** run `git commit` during spec stages — even for `docs: lock spec FINAL`.
4. **`/start-coding`**: stage with `git add`; print suggested message for user's commit after `/review-staged`.
5. **`/review-staged`**: review only; on READY → print commit command, do not execute.
6. **`/create-pr`**: generate title/body text only — user pushes when ready.
7. **NEVER** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or any agent co-author trailer to commit messages.
